  "type": "multiple-choice",
  "originalQuery": "Your team uses multiple Cloud SQL instances to support various internal applications. These instances experience peak load during weekdays and significantly lower usage during weekends. You want to optimize costs while ensuring availability during peak periods. What should you do?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Migrate the databases to a Compute Engine VM with a custom cron job for scheduling.<br/>B. Configure Cloud Scheduler to trigger a Cloud Function that resizes the instances during off-peak hours.<br/>C. Enable high availability for the Cloud SQL instances and monitor their utilization using Cloud Monitoring.<br/>D. Use a managed instance group (MIG) to automatically scale Cloud SQL instances up and down.",
  "domain": "Deploy scalable and highly available databases in Google Cloud",
  "hasImage": false,
